# Cross-origin isolation headers.
#
# The rayon thread pool runs on SharedArrayBuffer, which browsers only expose to
# cross-origin isolated documents. Without these headers every lab falls back to
# a single thread and `performance.now()` stays coarsely clamped, so the pages
# detect that and label their results, but the threaded measurements are simply
# unavailable.
#
# This file is read by Cloudflare Pages and Netlify. For other hosts see
# `coi-serviceworker.js`, which achieves the same from inside the page.

/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp

# WebAssembly must be served with its own MIME type for streaming instantiation.
/*.wasm
  Content-Type: application/wasm
